leonard@mimsy.umd.edu (Leonard Dickens) writes:
{L} What alignment do you favor?  It seems to me that the best alignment to be
{L} is Lawful, for the following reasons:
{L} 1) Two of the best artifacts (Mjollnir, Excaliber) available from god. 
{L} 2) Can convert any altar to Lawful, which is good because:
{L} 3) Lawful altars make holy water, i.e., blessings.

{L} Any dissention on this point?

Well since your asking (;-) let me lament my last *MEGA* game as a Healer
(lawful) to counter your opinion.


I stared off with a bit of luck finding speed boots and and a wand of make
invisible on the first level.  Later a throne yielded Stormbringer and it
was off to the castle.

With my 7 wishes I got:
	gray dragon scale
	gauntlets of dexteriy
	more speed boots (thanks Mr. Lich)
	ring of teleport control
	blindfold
	magic marker (I had 6 blank scrolls by this time)
	and .... (I forgot, but it was something necessary)

Well, the blindfold wish was necessary because I searched levels 1-26 3 times
and still nothing.  (I do not polypile.  My own silly limitation.)  I never
did find a blindfold until level 35 on the way out with the Amulet, coming
up from level 50!

Anywho while walking out of hell theres this nasty little bit of code that
randomly bops characters back down (instead of up) a few levels when the
"go up stairs".  That *sucked*!  I went through the same levels as much as
3 times, and if I were chaotic I'd have been long out of hell.  Well in
the end (after about my 7th enounter with the Wiz) he got me by cloning
and calling in a few dragons.

ARGH!

I, of late, had been under the impression that "lawfuls" had an unfair
advantage in this game (due to holy water), but with this experience I'm
not so sure.

						- Norm.

P.S.  I was playing with a different strategy than usual.  Normally I explore
      all ~20 levels of hell before going after the Wiz (and digging out paths
      out of the mazes to the stairs).  But I was trying to see how much of
      as challenge it was this way.  Man is it a *lot* harder. although
      it took *hours* off of play time.

P.P.S.  Whoever suggested gauntlets of dex. over gauntlets of power I strongly
        disagree.  I (can you believe it) never found a scroll of enchant armor
        in the game so my +0 gauntlets of dex did very little for me.  Perhaps
        discovery of the enchant armor scroll should be a prereq before
        wishing for those.  In the end the loss of damage capabilities
        (I know) hurt my melee, and helped my death.
